nt  Trump is too friendly to President Putin  and they're holding a meeting with only  interpreters would mean nobody knows  what said nobody knows what's promised  nobody knows if there are any  concessions made particularly on the US  side toward the Russian side something  like a promise that you know the u.s.  doesn't really need to participate in  NATO exercises that would protect the  Baltic States that was one big worry  also on what might happen in Syria they  were  very worried about you know what what  President Trump may want to walk away  with some kind of victory from the  Russian president and what might be up  for grabs for President Putin in that in  that situation so I think that that was  the biggest drama that meeting went on  longer than scheduled two hours with  just those two men in the room and we'll  we'll never know exactly what was said  and then of course the meeting with  advisors also longer than expected we  waited a long time on that picture of  waiting for the press conference and I  think that um they didn't disappoint I  think we expected them to come out both  declaring victory and I think that's  exactly what we heard all right and  Terry that is exactly what makes this so  very difficult is that there is no  official record of what's been said so  we just have to go by what these two  leaders have said teri Schultz reporting  live from Helsinki thank you
 

